# Typing Generic Responses

## When to use
- Designing HTTP response shapes
- Defining use-case return types
- Creating persistence ports (Repository interfaces)

## Core rules
1. `ApiResponse<T>` for all HTTP responses (success + error envelope)
2. `Result<T,E>` for use-case outputs (typed success/error without throwing)
3. `Paginated<T>` for list endpoint responses
4. `Repository<T,ID>` generic interface for persistence ports
5. All cross-boundary types are explicit, no `any` or `object`

## Reference shape (TypeScript)

### ApiResponse<T>
```typescript
export interface ApiResponse<T = unknown> {
  readonly success: boolean;
  readonly data?: T;
  readonly error?: { code: string; message: string; details?: Record<string, unknown> };
  readonly metadata?: { timestamp: string; traceId: string };
}
```

### Result<T,E>
```typescript
export type Result<T, E extends AppError = AppError> =
  | { readonly success: true; readonly value: T }
  | { readonly success: false; readonly error: E };

export const ok = <T>(value: T): Result<T, never> => ({ success: true, value });
export const err = <E extends AppError>(error: E): Result<never, E> => ({ success: false, error });
```

### Repository<T,ID>
```typescript
export interface Repository<T, ID> {
  findById(id: ID): Promise<T | null>;
  save(entity: T): Promise<T>;
  deleteById(id: ID): Promise<boolean>;
}
```

## Examples — Do
```typescript
// Use-case returns Result
async execute(id: string): Promise<Result<User, NotFoundError>> {
  const user = await this.repo.findById(id);
  return user ? ok(user) : err(new NotFoundError('User', id));
}
```

## Examples — Don't
```typescript
// ❌ No typing
async findUser(id: string): Promise<any> { ... }
// ❌ Direct HTTP response from use-case
return res.status(200).json({ data: user });
```

## Checklist
- [ ] `ApiResponse<T>` used for all HTTP responses
- [ ] `Result<T,E>` used for use-case returns
- [ ] `Repository<T,ID>` generic interface defined
- [ ] No `any` in cross-boundary types

See [reference/generic-patterns.md](./reference/generic-patterns.md) for full patterns.

