## Summary Table

| Pattern | Category | Use When |
|---------|-----------|----------|
| Abstract Factory | Creational | Create families of related objects |
| Builder | Creational | Construct complex objects step by step |
| Prototype | Creational | Clone objects efficiently |
| Singleton | Creational | One instance (avoid — use DI) |
| Adapter | Structural | Make incompatible interfaces work together |
| Bridge | Structural | Decouple abstraction from implementation |
| Composite | Structural | Treat tree structures uniformly |
| Facade | Structural | Simplify complex subsystem with simple interface |
| Proxy | Structural | Control access to object |
| Chain of Responsibility | Behavioral | Pass request along chain of handlers |
| Command | Behavioral | Encapsulate request as object with undo |
| Iterator | Behavioral | Access elements sequentially |
| Mediator | Behavioral | Centralize communication between objects |
| Memento | Behavioral | Capture and restore object state |
| State | Behavioral | Alter behavior when state changes |
| Template Method | Behavioral | Define skeleton, let subclasses override steps |
| Visitor | Behavioral | Add operations to object structure without changing classes |
| Unit of Work | Enterprise | Track changes and commit as single transaction |
| CQRS | Enterprise | Separate read and write models |
| Event Sourcing | Enterprise | Store state as sequence of events |

# Code Comment Patterns — Standards, Syntax, Best Practices

## 1. General Rules

### Do's
- [ ] Write comments for **why**, not **what** (code already shows what)
- [ ] Use JSDoc for public APIs (classes, methods, interfaces)
- [ ] Keep comments up to date with code changes
- [ ] Write comments in English
- [ ] Use complete sentences for block comments

### Don'ts
- [ ] No commented-out code (use version control instead)
- [ ] No redundant comments (`i++ // increment i`)
- [ ] No joke comments or personal notes
- [ ] No TODO without ticket reference (`TODO(#123): ...`)
- [ ] No `// @ts-ignore` without justification comment

---

## 2. JSDoc Syntax (For Public APIs)

### Class Documentation
```typescript
/**
 * User domain entity.
 * Represents a registered user with authentication and authorization capabilities.
 *
 * @remarks
 * This entity enforces invariants: email uniqueness, password strength.
 * Use {@link User.create} factory method to instantiate.
 *
 * @example
 * ```typescript
 * const email = Email.create('test@example.com');
 * const user = User.create('1', email, hashedPassword);
 * ```
 */
export class User {
  // ...
}
```

### Method Documentation
```typescript
/**
 * Creates a new user with the given email and password.
 *
 * @param id - Unique identifier for the user
 * @param email - Valid email address (validated by Email value object)
 * @param passwordHash - Bcrypt hashed password (never store plain text)
 * @returns A new User instance
 * @throws {ValidationError} If email is invalid
 * @throws {DuplicateUserError} If user with email already exists
 *
 * @example
 * ```typescript
 * const user = User.create('1', Email.create('test@example.com'), hash);
 * ```
 */
static create(id: string, email: Email, passwordHash: string): User {
  return new User(id, email, passwordHash);
}
```

### Interface Documentation
```typescript
/**
 * Port for user persistence.
 * Implemented by infrastructure layer (TypeORM, Prisma, etc.).
 *
 * @typeParam T - Entity type (User)
 * @typeParam ID - Identifier type (string)
 */
export interface UserRepository extends Repository<User, string> {
  /**
   * Finds a user by their email address.
   * @param email - Email address to search for
   * @returns User if found, null otherwise
   */
  findByEmail(email: string): Promise<User | null>;
}
```

---

## 3. Inline Comments (Single Line)

### Format
```typescript
// Good: explains why
// Using Set to ensure O(1) lookup for user roles
const roleSet = new Set(user.roles);

// Good: explains non-obvious logic
// Sort by priority descending, then by createdAt ascending
items.sort((a, b) => b.priority - a.priority || a.createdAt - b.createdAt);

// Bad: states the obvious
// Increment i
i++;

// Bad: commented out code
// TODO: remove this later
// const oldLogic = ...;
```

### TODO/FIXME/HACK Comments
```typescript
// TODO(#123): Add rate limiting for this endpoint
// FIXME(#456): Temporary workaround for TypeORM bug, remove after upgrade
// HACK: Direct DB query needed because TypeORM doesn't support this query yet
```

